# Neo Mallet parameters (docs/specs/neo-mallet.md). The order changes only with a version (machines.md §3.2): songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoMallet
namespace NeoBuzz.Mallet
class NeoMalletMachine
tracks 16
summary A modal synth for mallets, bars, bells and plucks: each note rings a bank of up to 32 decaying modes (soft, hard, metal and bright bars, a tube, a bell, a tine, a stiff string, glass, a plate, or a custom stretched series), struck by a mallet whose contact time sets how much of the highs it excites, at a position along the body that weighs each mode, or plucked. Decay, a damping tilt that kills the highs sooner, brightness, a tremolo, release damping and velocity to hardness shape it. 16 voices. Use it for marimba, vibraphone and glockenspiel, chimes, bells, music-box tines, harp-like plucks and glass pads.

group Model
Model       "Model"         0 10    0     enum Soft_bar Hard_bar Metal_bar Bright_bar Tube Bell Tine Pluck Glass Plate Custom | The body: which modes the note rings (their frequency ratios and weights)
    how Chooses the body that rings: a soft (marimba-like) bar, a hard (xylophone-like) bar, a metal (vibraphone-like) bar, a bright (glockenspiel-like) bar, a tube, a bell, a tine, a stiff string, glass, a plate, or a custom stretched series.
    sound Bars are woody or metallic and pitched, the tube is hollow, the bell is deep with a minor-third shimmer, the tine is thin and sweet, the string is plucked, glass beats slowly and the plate is clangorous.
group Exciter
Hardness    "Hardness"      0 1000  486   exp 12 0.3 ms 1                 | The mallet's contact time with the body, 12 ms (a soft felt head) down to 0.3 ms (a hard stick): a short contact excites the high modes, a long one only the low
    how Sets how hard the mallet is, from a soft head that touches the bar for 12 ms to a hard stick that touches it for 0.3 ms. The knob reads the contact time.
    sound Soft heads give a round, dull thud with few overtones; hard sticks give a bright, clicking, ringing attack.
Position    "Position"      0 1000  300   pct                             | Where along the body the mallet strikes: each mode n is weighed by the sine of n times pi times the position (bells, glass and plates by their own shape), so a mode at a node is nearly silent
    how Moves the strike across the body from one end (0 %) to the other (100 %).
    sound The centre brings out the fundamental and hides the second mode; towards the ends the overtones take over and the tone turns thin and nasal.
VelHard     "Velocity to hardness" 0 1000 600 pct                        | How much the note's velocity changes the contact time: at 100 % a hard hit (velocity 127) is about 8 times shorter, and a soft hit 8 times longer, than the Hardness setting
    how Sets how much a hard hit also makes the mallet harder, from 0 % (velocity only changes the level) to 100 %.
    sound Soft hits are dull and quiet, hard hits bright and loud, as with a real mallet.
Noise       "Mallet noise"  0 1000  100   pct                             | The share of noise in the strike, a short burst shaped by the contact: the sound of the mallet's own impact
    how Sets how much noise the strike adds, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A little adds the knock of the mallet on the wood; a lot makes a breathy, clacking attack.
group Decay
Decay       "Decay"         0 1000  616   time 0.05 20                    | Decay time of the fundamental, the time it takes to fall by 60 dB (T60)
    how Sets how long the fundamental rings, as the time to fall by 60 dB, from 0.05 to 20 s.
    sound Short times are dry wooden knocks; long times ring like metal bars, bells and chimes.
Tilt        "Damping tilt"  0 1000  500   pct                             | How much sooner the high modes die than the fundamental: at 100 % a mode twice as high decays in a quarter of the time (a model that rings on in the highs, such as the metal bar, uses less)
    how Sets how much faster the high modes fade than the fundamental, from 0 % (all modes ring as long as the fundamental) to 100 %.
    sound More tilt gives a warm, quick-darkening note; less keeps the sparkle ringing.
Bright      "Brightness"    0 1000  500   bip                             | Tilts the level of the modes with frequency: +100 % raises each octave up by 6 dB, -100 % lowers it by 6 dB
    how Sets the balance between low and high modes, from -100 % (dark) to +100 % (bright).
    sound Down it is round and dull; up it is glassy and edgy.
Release     "Release damping" 0 1000 683  exp 5 2000 ms 0               | How fast a released note is damped: the time for it to fall by 60 dB after the key goes up (a stopped note is faded in at least 3 ms)
    how Sets how quickly letting go of a key stops the sound, from 5 ms (a hand on the bar) to 2 s.
    sound Short times stop the note at once like a damper; long times let notes ring out as on an open instrument.
group Modes
Modes       "Modes"         0 28    12    int 4                     | How many modes each note rings, 4 to 32 (modes above 0.45 of the sample rate are dropped)
    how Sets the number of modes in each note's body, from 4 to 32.
    sound Few modes sound plain and cheap to play; many modes sound rich and complex.
Stretch     "Stretch"       0 1000  500   lin -50 50 ct 1                 | Custom model: each mode is this many cents higher than a harmonic series would put it, per mode number step (0 is a harmonic series, positive bends it bell-like)
    how Bends the Custom series: how many cents each mode is pushed per step of its number.
    sound Zero sounds like an organ pipe or a plucked string; more turns it into a bell, less into something hollow.
Inharm      "Inharmonicity" 0 1000  0     pct                             | Stiff-string and Custom models: the inharmonicity B of a stiff string, mode n sits at n times the fundamental times the square root of one plus B times n squared, with B = 0.02 times the setting squared, so B = 0.02 at 100 %
    how Sets the stiffness of the string, from 0 (a perfect harmonic series) to 100 % (B = 0.02, a stiff piano bass string and beyond).
    sound A little makes the string sound real and slightly bright; a lot makes it clang.
group Tremolo
TremRate    "Tremolo rate"  0 1000  691   exp 0.5 12 Hz 2                 | Rate of the tremolo, the level swing of a vibraphone's rotating fans
    how Sets the speed of the tremolo from 0.5 to 12 Hz.
    sound Slow is a gentle swell; fast is a flutter.
TremDepth   "Tremolo depth" 0 1000  0     pct                             | Depth of the tremolo: at 100 % the level swings between full and silent
    how Sets how deeply the level swings, from 0 % (off) to 100 %.
    sound Turn it up for the pulsing of a vibraphone with its motor on.
group Output
Spread      "Stereo spread" 0 1000  400   pct                             | How far the notes are placed left and right by their pitch (0 % is all centre)
    how Sets how widely low and high notes are spread across the stereo field, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Like a real instrument seen from the front, low bars sit left and high bars right.
Volume      "Volume"        0 1000  750   db -60 12 inf                   | Output level
    how Sets the final level in dB, from off to +12.
    sound It makes the instrument louder or quieter without changing its character.
